-releases-ios-8-gm-ahead-of-sep-17-public-release" class="external text" id="mwAr4">Archived</a> from the original on May 13, 2019<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwAr8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwAsA">December 30,</span> 2016</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=9to5Mac&amp;rft.atitle=Apple+releases+iOS+8+GM+ahead+of+Sep.+17+public+release&amp;rft.date=2014-09-09&amp;rft.aulast=Hall&amp;rft.aufirst=Zac&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2F9to5mac.com%2F2014%2F09%2F09%2Fapple-releases-ios-8-gm-ahead-of-sep-17-public-release&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AIOS+7" class="Z3988" about="#mwt7" id="mwAsE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-2" id="cite_note-2" data-mw-footnote-number="2"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAsI"><a href="#cite_ref-2" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAsM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAsQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-2" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt10" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAsU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite web","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.engadget.com/2013-09-10-ios-7-64-bit.html"},"title":{"wt":"iOS 7 will be 64-bit, just like the iPhone 5s&apos; new A7 chip"},"date":{"wt":"September 10, 2013"},"publisher":{"wt":"engadget"},"last":{"wt":"Wollman"},"first":{"wt":"Dana"},"access-date":{"wt":"January 3, 2023"},"archive-date":{"wt":"December 20, 2020"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20201220042920/https://www.engadget.com/2013-09-10-ios-7-64-bit.html"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFWollman2013" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt10">Wollman, Dana (September 10, 2013). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.engadget.com/2013-09-10-ios-7-64-bit.html" class="external text" id="mwAsY">"iOS 7 will be 64-bit, just like the iPhone 5s' new A7 chip"</a>. engadget. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20201220042920/https://www.engadget.com/2013-09-10-ios-7-64-bit.html" class="external text" id="mwAsc">Archived</a> from the original on December 20, 2020<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwAsg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwAsk">January 3,</span> 2023</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=iOS+7+will+be+64-bit%2C+just+like+the+iPhone+5s%27+new+A7+chip&amp;rft.pub=engadget&amp;rft.date=2013-09-10&amp;rft.aulast=Wollman&amp;rft.aufirst=Dana&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.engadget.com%2F2013-09-10-ios-7-64-bit.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AIOS+7" class="Z3988" about="#mwt10" id="mwAso"></span></span></li>
